From: Pear contributors
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: reject unsupported generated stubs and unwind failed imports

Original Pear integration against Wine 4e819f054dd2d9ee855ee3f1e30d8c1bb8f80fcf
with preceding ordered Pear patches. In the configured native PE publication
path, propagate typed missing-export failures, check and restore IAT protection,
and reuse the existing loader dependency graph and unload machinery before
removing failed-module bookkeeping. Preserve upstream behavior outside that
configuration. Original callback DLL fixtures exercise real held references
through direct NtCallbackReturn; no arbitrary dangling-pointer safety is claimed.
Existing Wine LGPL-2.1-or-later notices apply.

